{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309...2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309...2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","permalink_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/OmniNode-ai:65c237c...OmniNode-ai:2f654f8","diff_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309...2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309...2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","node_id":"C_kwDOR6jjtdoAKDY1YzIzN2NkYzkxNGE2YzdjMWUxNWRlMzA4OTg2ZWM2NWMyNGYzMDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-09-14T07:53:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-14T07:53:56Z"},"message":"fix(OMN-18349): feed the golden corpus at the rate the lane actually serves (#2538)\n\nThe first nightly run that reached the lane (34810939133) published all nine\ncases at once under one deadline, on a comment reading \"the platform is expected\nto serve them concurrently\". It is not, and three declarations already said so:\n\n  * the delegate-skill command consumer's poll loop is serial -- it awaits each\n    dispatch before requesting the next record;\n  * the tier every case enters on is one physical endpoint permitting one\n    running generation;\n  * a handler that hits its execution budget stops WAITING for its delegation,\n    it does not stop the delegation, so each abandoned workflow went on\n    competing for that single slot.\n\nMeasured on that run's own projection rows: cases three through seven were each\ncancelled at an exact 240.000s cadence -- 06:00:37.87, 06:04:37.88, 06:08:37.88,\n06:12:37.89, 06:16:37.89 -- every one having spent its whole budget behind work\nthe probe had already given up on.\n\nThe per-case deadline was also taken from the wrong contract:\nnode_delegation_orchestrator's completion_bound (900s), a real bound for a node\nthat does not serve this probe. The node that does is\nnode_delegate_skill_orchestrator, whose handler_execution_budget (240s,\nOMN-15504) is what terminalises a case. 660 of those 900 seconds were spent\nwaiting for an event the platform had already decided not to produce. That the\ntwo declared bounds disagree is a real finding and is NOT resolved here.\n\nAnd the empty rows those cancellations produce were being reported as the wrong\ndefect. delegation_events carries no terminal_state and no status column, so\nrow_terminal defaulted every row to \"completed\" and a cancelled delegation was\nscored against the completed-row expectations as \"tokens: expected positive, got\ninput=0 output=0\" -- a description of the OMN-13535 telemetry-drop regression,\nwhich was not happening. Five of nine cases were misreported that way.\n\nChanges:\n  * the corpus is published in waves sized to the entry tier's declared\n    max_concurrent_generations, each wave drained before the next is published;\n  * that number is now a field on the saturation policy rather than a sentence\n    in its header, and an undeclared one RAISES rather than defaulting;\n  * the per-case deadline reads the handler execution budget of the node that\n    serves the probe;\n  * a budget-timeout row is classified as terminal \"timeout\" and reported as a\n    named delegation timeout quoting the budget;\n  * delegation_events is an upsert, so a budget-timeout row is given the\n    declared projection margin to be superseded -- correlation id 0df23c72\n    projected empty at 05:56:37.886Z and the real terminal, 77/1819 tokens and\n    the gate passed, landed 12.9 seconds later over the top of it;\n  * timeout-minutes goes 45 -> 70, and scripts/ci/check_nightly_corpus_budget.py\n    recomputes the ceiling from the corpus, the contract and the overlay using\n    the probe's own arithmetic and fails if the budget is below it -- a job\n    cancelled mid-corpus skips its if: always() uploads and leaves a red night\n    with no scoreboard, which is AC3 failing by another route.\n\nWired as the nightly-corpus-budget pre-commit hook AND\ntests/test_delegation_nightly_budget.py inside the required pytest job, same\npredicate both sides.\n\nFalsification controls run, each restored byte-identical afterwards: restoring\nthe fan-out publish turns the interleave test RED at \"assert 9 <= 1\"; restoring\nthe old terminal default reproduces the live misreport string verbatim;\nremoving the supersession window returns the stale empty row; restoring the\nother node's completion bound turns both deadline tests RED and drives the\nderived ceiling from 59 to 158 minutes. Committed positive controls cover an\nundeclared concurrency, an ordinary row still reading \"completed\", a never-\nsuperseded row, and a budget above the ceiling.\n\npre-commit run --all-files exit 0 across 92 hooks, mypy src/ --strict clean.","tree":{"sha":"856a43d8274b3fca5dab7cc24963b38b38db2b52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/trees/856a43d8274b3fca5dab7cc24963b38b38db2b52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/commits/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp6gUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC+4QABz8ViaTlObPhmyOnrT/JzmC\nXByl2hlmh0UrmJjWNVEEXZxwMf/3KEO0v++L97Ra17zN5V9G3BuXzo33ojc0jNIs\nbhLQkf1+7G2dropRwSLTMmrCbSGOZlyq/eIxb1w8/nMhQhr+ESp92ICfw7ySTVqo\n6A6gCsqwitJa0sShrxYH3TozCp62a+lBKxILjrwSfSJhm4JXeqGp+ARX314a4XR2\nE5MuYxUu8zAVz4MraHumBt+qJVJThP+7Jvv3U8KJHj+7nNRwhFL+kXDnlh0wPdIx\ntqDpj0C2EJd7Uc52bK46EjYueQSTTRW60cD3cBWCaHJUt2q4WWpeYcf+Vm83TBzY\nT5ih5fCBCO6EHXTX6Qg859XmXkDIvQM6DtG0KSC/LxuVX8t0MLgTQrHGcewpwZzr\n+/eor5DTDTZccyA7MRHQSu4uLwr+ckcMLL61XFpyUdYzv/NiR8QNl7YgX9O2a3uu\nTb9I4jXzchznJYyPbCbwrmhR5kFKXuFXclYYeVgeQamcUKG0dNX6bltwuN95JbZJ\nRNM4m69kW8elB1JA6HZzcBpBQNV1nFBoCt4pm3th/yJ+IM5uNAlPkcFRUNyb7QAH\nBdyHWphD5e/lQIsKDu3T9Z810E1kBSO4ARfT07obWQCc8VhJoVNATPFp12MJFABz\nx8YyMpz9Zq3p4ddObYhB\n=ZM9r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 856a43d8274b3fca5dab7cc24963b38b38db2b52\nparent 1b5a6c4b6061804140fe1582061f345e0f973937\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1789372436 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789372436 +0000\n\nfix(OMN-18349): feed the golden corpus at the rate the lane actually serves (#2538)\n\nThe first nightly run that reached the lane (34810939133) published all nine\ncases at once under one deadline, on a comment reading \"the platform is expected\nto serve them concurrently\". It is not, and three declarations already said so:\n\n  * the delegate-skill command consumer's poll loop is serial -- it awaits each\n    dispatch before requesting the next record;\n  * the tier every case enters on is one physical endpoint permitting one\n    running generation;\n  * a handler that hits its execution budget stops WAITING for its delegation,\n    it does not stop the delegation, so each abandoned workflow went on\n    competing for that single slot.\n\nMeasured on that run's own projection rows: cases three through seven were each\ncancelled at an exact 240.000s cadence -- 06:00:37.87, 06:04:37.88, 06:08:37.88,\n06:12:37.89, 06:16:37.89 -- every one having spent its whole budget behind work\nthe probe had already given up on.\n\nThe per-case deadline was also taken from the wrong contract:\nnode_delegation_orchestrator's completion_bound (900s), a real bound for a node\nthat does not serve this probe. The node that does is\nnode_delegate_skill_orchestrator, whose handler_execution_budget (240s,\nOMN-15504) is what terminalises a case. 660 of those 900 seconds were spent\nwaiting for an event the platform had already decided not to produce. That the\ntwo declared bounds disagree is a real finding and is NOT resolved here.\n\nAnd the empty rows those cancellations produce were being reported as the wrong\ndefect. delegation_events carries no terminal_state and no status column, so\nrow_terminal defaulted every row to \"completed\" and a cancelled delegation was\nscored against the completed-row expectations as \"tokens: expected positive, got\ninput=0 output=0\" -- a description of the OMN-13535 telemetry-drop regression,\nwhich was not happening. Five of nine cases were misreported that way.\n\nChanges:\n  * the corpus is published in waves sized to the entry tier's declared\n    max_concurrent_generations, each wave drained before the next is published;\n  * that number is now a field on the saturation policy rather than a sentence\n    in its header, and an undeclared one RAISES rather than defaulting;\n  * the per-case deadline reads the handler execution budget of the node that\n    serves the probe;\n  * a budget-timeout row is classified as terminal \"timeout\" and reported as a\n    named delegation timeout quoting the budget;\n  * delegation_events is an upsert, so a budget-timeout row is given the\n    declared projection margin to be superseded -- correlation id 0df23c72\n    projected empty at 05:56:37.886Z and the real terminal, 77/1819 tokens and\n    the gate passed, landed 12.9 seconds later over the top of it;\n  * timeout-minutes goes 45 -> 70, and scripts/ci/check_nightly_corpus_budget.py\n    recomputes the ceiling from the corpus, the contract and the overlay using\n    the probe's own arithmetic and fails if the budget is below it -- a job\n    cancelled mid-corpus skips its if: always() uploads and leaves a red night\n    with no scoreboard, which is AC3 failing by another route.\n\nWired as the nightly-corpus-budget pre-commit hook AND\ntests/test_delegation_nightly_budget.py inside the required pytest job, same\npredicate both sides.\n\nFalsification controls run, each restored byte-identical afterwards: restoring\nthe fan-out publish turns the interleave test RED at \"assert 9 <= 1\"; restoring\nthe old terminal default reproduces the live misreport string verbatim;\nremoving the supersession window returns the stale empty row; restoring the\nother node's completion bound turns both deadline tests RED and drives the\nderived ceiling from 59 to 158 minutes. Committed positive controls cover an\nundeclared concurrency, an ordinary row still reading \"completed\", a never-\nsuperseded row, and a budget above the ceiling.\n\npre-commit run --all-files exit 0 across 92 hooks, mypy src/ --strict clean.","verified_at":"2026-09-14T07:53:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":f