6:16:37.89 -- every one having spent its whole budget behind work\nthe probe had already given up on.\n\nThe per-case deadline was also taken from the wrong contract:\nnode_delegation_orchestrator's completion_bound (900s), a real bound for a node\nthat does not serve this probe. The node that does is\nnode_delegate_skill_orchestrator, whose handler_execution_budget (240s,\nOMN-15504) is what terminalises a case. 660 of those 900 seconds were spent\nwaiting for an event the platform had already decided not to produce. That the\ntwo declared bounds disagree is a real finding and is NOT resolved here.\n\nAnd the empty rows those cancellations produce were being reported as the wrong\ndefect. delegation_events carries no terminal_state and no status column, so\nrow_terminal defaulted every row to \"completed\" and a cancelled delegation was\nscored against the completed-row expectations as \"tokens: expected positive, got\ninput=0 output=0\" -- a description of the OMN-13535 telemetry-drop regression,\nwhich was not happening. Five of nine cases were misreported that way.\n\nChanges:\n  * the corpus is published in waves sized to the entry tier's declared\n    max_concurrent_generations, each wave drained before the next is published;\n  * that number is now a field on the saturation policy rather than a sentence\n    in its header, and an undeclared one RAISES rather than defaulting;\n  * the per-case deadline reads the handler execution budget of the node that\n    serves the probe;\n  * a budget-timeout row is classified as terminal \"timeout\" and reported as a\n    named delegation timeout quoting the budget;\n  * delegation_events is an upsert, so a budget-timeout row is given the\n    declared projection margin to be superseded -- correlation id 0df23c72\n    projected empty at 05:56:37.886Z and the real terminal, 77/1819 tokens and\n    the gate passed, landed 12.9 seconds later over the top of it;\n  * timeout-minutes goes 45 -> 70, and scripts/ci/check_nightly_corpus_budget.py\n    recomputes the ceiling from the corpus, the contract and the overlay using\n    the probe's own arithmetic and fails if the budget is below it -- a job\n    cancelled mid-corpus skips its if: always() uploads and leaves a red night\n    with no scoreboard, which is AC3 failing by another route.\n\nWired as the nightly-corpus-budget pre-commit hook AND\ntests/test_delegation_nightly_budget.py inside the required pytest job, same\npredicate both sides.\n\nFalsification controls run, each restored byte-identical afterwards: restoring\nthe fan-out publish turns the interleave test RED at \"assert 9 <= 1\"; restoring\nthe old terminal default reproduces the live misreport string verbatim;\nremoving the supersession window returns the stale empty row; restoring the\nother node's completion bound turns both deadline tests RED and drives the\nderived ceiling from 59 to 158 minutes. Committed positive controls cover an\nundeclared concurrency, an ordinary row still reading \"completed\", a never-\nsuperseded row, and a budget above the ceiling.\n\npre-commit run --all-files exit 0 across 92 hooks, mypy src/ --strict clean.","verified_at":"2026-09-14T07:53:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1b5a6c4b6061804140fe1582061f345e0f973937","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/1b5a6c4b6061804140fe1582061f345e0f973937","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/1b5a6c4b6061804140fe1582061f345e0f973937"}]},"status":"ahead","ahead_by":3,"behind_by":0,"total_commits":3,"commits":[{"sha":"4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f","node_id":"C_kwDOR6jjtdoAKDRiYzI0MzcyMTA5Mzk3MDJmYTBkYzg1MjkzNjJjMGE3YzIzMTA0OWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-09-14T09:11:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-14T09:11:34Z"},"message":"fix(OMN-18332): transcribe criterion bindings on the born mint path too (#2537)\n\n* fix(OMN-18332): transcribe criterion bindings on the born mint path too\n\nAC6. The transcription landed on one of the two producers that mint OCC\nevidence companions and was proven there; the other one, which mints the\nmajority, had no Linear read at all.\n\nMeasured on the deployed effects container between its 2026-09-14T03:38:44Z\nrestart and 06:1xZ: nine companions minted, seven carrying\n`runner: node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect` (the born path) and two carrying\n`runner: node_occ_companion_compute`, and not one of the nine carrying a\nbinds_ac key. Positive control: 65 contracts on OCC dev do carry one. The\ndeployed emitter contains zero occurrences of the string `ac_bindings` while\nthe renderer that would emit it sits unused in the emitter's own package.\n\nThe two compute-path companions are correct as minted: probed live through the\nruntime's own key, OMN-18033 and OMN-13912 declare no falsifiers and yield zero\nbindings. The born-path ones are not: OMN-18333 yields five bindings, four of\nthem accepted, from the same reader, and its companion claimed none of them.\n\nThe read now lives in one module, `omnimarket.occ_ticket_bindings`, imported by\nboth producers, so wiring it to one and missing the other is a deliberate act\nrather than the default. `render_companion_contract` and\n`render_downstream_dod_evidence_item` take `ac_bindings` and render it on the\ndownstream item exactly where the compute twin renders it; the F-04 repair path\ntakes the same records, so a second companion on a shared ticket cannot bind\nwhere the first one did not. Empty renders bytes identical to today, so a\nLinear outage or a ticket that declared no falsifiers costs the bindings and\nnever the mint.\n\nRED first: nine tests failed against the unwired tree, nine pass now. 964\npassed / 12 skipped across the four affected node suites plus the occ unit\nsuite; mypy --strict and pre-commit clean.\n\n* fix(OMN-18332): home the shared reader inside the effect that owns the transport\n\nThe first commit put the shared Linear read at `src/omnimarket/occ_ticket_bindings.py`,\nwhich the imperative-contract guard correctly refused: a raw HTTP call from a\nfreestanding `src/` module is exactly the violation it blocks (OMN-12515). Verified\nby running the guard locally against this worktree -- exit 1 naming\n`occ_ticket_bindings.py: hybrid (live)` at the urlopen line, exit 0 with no blocking\nsection after the move, same command, same allowlists, no allowlist entry added.\n\nThe module now sits beside `occ_evidence_stamp.py` in the born-path effect's\nhandlers package, which is where the OCC authoring helpers already live and where\n`node_occ_companion_compute` already imports them from -- so the read follows the\ncross-node dependency direction that exists rather than adding a second one, and\nthe transport sits inside an EFFECT where it belongs.\n\n964 passed / 12 skipped across the four affected node suites plus the occ unit\nsuite; mypy --strict and pre-commit clean.","tree":{"sha":"ee6d60a49e1f71bcb7da1cb5efa5f42f3928aa2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/trees/ee6d60a49e1f71bcb7da1cb5efa5f42f3928aa2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/commits/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp7pGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGiEQABhDIzycve6/yRUskBicfr8r\nCFa0zcycggh9/0ZJU/e2AiTzFFV21dLYCBDDggkNFfl4AuB0Hvb9xk6oJEHJO6lU\nfNJsJmtaypzQlWFqDrtGsE9N0ODOE/Eft5p1Qb0RdVa68+3QuKwSlgESDb9Tsrbg\nJp0XaS+13XEt/hEXtv76s471PZpqemakOH1qs0mZgKwPYiIRfoLyN7S28Zutt7ho\nMU6//6Wrt9ZCGQvlrXCy5eowKgM9rzFXKyX3OXxH0h7XIsTajinlkXdvVGgxX1bS\nohnZvrC5GXrPCTbs3oq0DhQM7jh7se8ECe0AOexqdhf8Q/HHukonHMtKI0dKnCPF\nqXx+IDekdv5vu+yaU5i9CDZfB48BtID9VYdqVDBGIgE8LeEcWiThI9r3ApXVyfPl\nsv2yUdOJAFljU1hi9nDuHCW34CFuD9qVaVQV0KqgMcmpUCsucRGD/VBTyqugud6d\nmWer5R9yxxP0gkdQzLVCgVnud2dsN8HMO4rdDmshBOZGpI8G4T8zs1nbmdsEm0al\nIg720BE40OoTWui0vA58vR+ur+L1TqljDwDRzuS0FDmoWWUellY2r8Wp191/487z\nt5s0PAeZEs8yuKxBMI/pFjSWIW9ibAiH/W7xqMI3yo0FQfwPI36/W3ijTBzi8Krp\nM1nHhgSgTcI6KWyQiKjF\n=QxWs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ee6d60a49e1f71bcb7da1cb5efa5f42f3928aa2c\nparent 65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1789377094 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789377094 +0000\n\nfix(OMN-18332): transcribe criterion bindings on the born mint path too (#2537)\n\n* fix(OMN-18332): transcribe criterion bindings on the born mint path too\n\nAC6. The transcription landed on one of the two producers that mint OCC\nevidence companions and was proven there; the other one, which mints the\nmajority, had no Linear read at all.\n\nMeasured on the deployed effects container between its 2026-09-14T03:38:44Z\nrestart and 06:1xZ: nine companions minted, seven carrying\n`runner: node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect` (the born path) and two carrying\n`runner: node_occ_companion_compute`, and not one of the nine carrying a\nbinds_ac key. Positive control: 65 contracts on OCC dev do carry one. The\ndeployed emitter contains zero occurrences of the string `ac_bindings` while\nthe renderer that would emit it sits unused in the emitter's own package.\n\nThe two compute-path companions are correct as minted: probed live through the\nruntime's own key, OMN-18033 and OMN-13912 declare no falsifiers and yield zero\nbindings. The born-path ones are not: OMN-18333 yields five bindings, four of\nthem accepted, from the same reader, and its companion claimed none of them.\n\nThe read now lives in one module, `omnimarket.occ_ticket_bindings`, imported by\nboth producers, so wiring it to one and missing the other is a deliberate act\nrather than the default. `render_companion_contract` and\n`render_downstream_dod_evidence_item` take `ac_bindings` and render it on the\ndownstream item exactly where the compute twin renders it; the F-04 repair path\ntakes the same records, so a second companion on a shared ticket cannot bind\nwhere the first one did not. Empty renders bytes identical to today, so a\nLinear outage or a ticket that declared no falsifiers costs the bindings and\nnever the mint.\n\nRED first: nine tests failed against the unwired tree, nine pass now. 964\npassed / 12 skipped across the four affected node suites plus the occ unit\nsuite; mypy --strict and pre-commit clean.\n\n* fix(OMN-18332): home the shared reader inside the effect that owns the transport\n\nThe first commit put the shared Linear read at `src/omnimarket/occ_ticket_bindings.py`,\nwhich the imperative-contract guard correctly refused: a raw HTTP call from a\nfreestanding `src/` module is exactly the violation it blocks (OMN-12515). Verified\nby running the guard locally against this worktree -- exit 1 naming\n`occ_ticket_bindings.py: hybrid (live)` at the urlopen line, exit 0 with no blocking\nsection after the move, same command, same allowlists, no allowlist entry added.\n\nThe module now sits beside `occ_evidence_stamp.py` in the born-path effect's\nhandlers package, which is where the OCC authoring helpers already live and where\n`node_occ_companion_compute` already imports them from -- so the read follows the\ncross-node dependency direction that exists rather than adding a second one, and\nthe transport sits inside an EFFECT where it belongs.\n\n964 passed / 12 skipped across the four affected node suites plus the occ unit\nsuite; mypy --strict and pre-commit clean.","verified_at":"2026-09-14T09:11:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309"}]},{"sha":"92a3cd1e5e59e31441f77e689ca928caa1624ad9","node_id":"C_kwDOR6jjtdoAKDkyYTNjZDFlNWU1OWUzMTQ0MWY3N2U2ODljYTkyOGNhYTE2MjRhZDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"onexbot-occ-writer[bot]","email":"307849072+onexbot-occ-writer[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-09-14T09:22:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-14T09:22:44Z"},"message":"chore(release): open dev for v0.4.82 [release-on-merge] (#2539)\n\nDisarms the OMN-16344 release-identity gate that publishing\nv0.4.81 armed against dev.\n\nTriggered-by: https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/actions/runs/34820002907\n\nCo-authored-by: onexbot-occ-writer[bot] <onexbot-occ-writer[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f6d08ae08173ecf50518080136125172143b5fa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/trees/f6d08ae08173ecf50518080136125172143b5fa7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/commits/92a3cd1e5e59e31441f77e689ca928caa1624ad9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp7zkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8ecQAAWSbugCUdbROUHalafV1A1k\nVtkxn3vyExn3PI8Oozk45iE0V3GHeBFpA0uj1Z7pDu+LVdyknnz6HRQ3p9u3kRdv\n7A8qMQvmCpeb+Vh1P4FBN6qcm+OWC5M5D1MyMNCFGMoG9eLw0u4zJVvIOEiG+c2T\nnL3Z7mXsSynvDllhXIyKxGyS6HP7//xuPQoTZznSMa1n1NcxmVXRFd/ezX6USQr+\nrR/zjhIGplrNhUBS9PFy1Zt8D7LEEelR3RQtGOhqE8GRtMMWH0tQ2/hzREwSf/wD\npGKK1lLMUyC0tStKu9yw4f93eOhrQ+TLR06Y6PG9/jP/gK4KfiZnXMiRxTRinpD1\nTxcJCYG5CJHt5uTfDo8y7dgMu1VXiAyB8yOK39v2d+Pse96dlcHHejzZglowbgS0\nHuaiUV+Hh/ie/XB5qfCgIvEZPtJ06bNKadTo5U5hKuKGXDD2ospd8vzHoMpWSKCj\n0CaSXNHL0pfmeET4rapnPEJIqZk4euiwZ9PAQ8QQMwROjpyHjezJHA0nzuv/p4Or\nWf1Fdqo3tWGYSG6TjMCtbxy76xgSGoLkDNZuwjjqpu+JVr2W+hyJf2FMiMmR3XSB\n+C6L/Aqdzg4dJlGwuNiGHJBQ4H8J9gA/Kp9pxHGlbqtGOg7LYjHq8mUu/A9ZRIJT\nMAXNRupHOWgvj6al71Fq\n=BEEK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f6d08ae08173ecf50518080136125172143b5fa7\nparent 4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f\nauthor onexbot-occ-writer[bot] <307849072+onexbot-occ-writer[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1789377764 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789377764 +0000\n\nchore(release): open dev for v0.4.82 [release-on-merge] (#2539)\n\nDisarms the OMN-16344 release-identity gate that publishing\nv0.4.81 armed against dev.\n\nTriggered-by: https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/actions/runs/34820002907\n\nCo-authored-by: onexbot-occ-writer[bot] <onexbot-occ-writer[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-09-14T09:22:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/92a3cd1e5e59e31441f77e689ca928caa1624ad9","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/92a3cd1e5e59e31441f77e689ca928caa1624ad9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/92a3cd1e5e59e31441f77e689ca928caa1624ad9/comments","author":{"login":"onexbot-occ-writer[bot]","id":307849072,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOEllncA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209038818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/onexbot-occ-writer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f"}]},{"sha":"2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","node_id":"C_kwDOR6jjtdoAKDJmNjU0ZjhkODY3M2I0NzAzYjkxOWZkODAxMjQxZTcwOTFkNjQ2ZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-09-14T10:09:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-14T10:09:56Z"},"message":"fix(OMN-18356): re-vendor criterion_units() suffix-label fix (#2540)\n\n* fix(OMN-18356): re-vendor criterion_units() suffix-label fix from omniclaude\n\nRe-derives the vendored _CRITERION_LABEL grammar and criterion_units()\nlabel construction from omniclaude's OMN-18356 fix (pending merge as\nomniclaude#2155): a suffixed ordinal (AC2b, AC10a) now binds as its own\nCriterionUnit instead of parsing UNLABELLED and being dropped by the\ntranscriber.\n\nFound live transcribing OMN-18332 (lane omn18332-autobinder-transcribe):\n6 of its 12 criteria (AC2b/c/d/e/f/g) parsed unlabelled and never reached\ntranscribe_ac_bindings() at all.\n\nRED first: a new test module (test_omn_18356_criterion_label_suffix.py)\nproves the defect at both levels -- the vendored parser directly, and the\nfull transcribe_ac_bindings() pipeline -- against the unfixed vendored\ncopy (verified via git stash of the source change), then GREEN after\nre-applying it. The pinned-span snapshot fixture is updated in the same\nchange so the clone-free drift leg (hosted CI) passes against the new\nvendored bytes.\n\nVENDORED_FROM_REVISION is NOT bumped in this commit: it still names\n3b1c66e787d3f45634ead74f8f10da7d8d02d54d (the OMN-18331 revision), which\ndoes not yet contain the OMN-18356 fix. The clone leg\n(TestPinnedSnapshotMatchesUpstream) therefore fails locally as expected\nuntil the pin is bumped to omniclaude#2155's merge squash in a follow-up\ncommit once that PR lands -- per the standing sequencing rule (the\nomniclaude PR merges first, and its squash is cited here). Holding this\nbranch unopened as a PR until that squash exists rather than opening one\nthat cites a pending, unmerged reference.\n\nTicket: OMN-18356\nGate: OMN-18328 AC-5\n\n* fix(OMN-18356): bump VENDORED_FROM_REVISION to omniclaude#2159's squash\n\nomniclaude#2159 merged as squash 7d3e5956451f045b68b726e1ea5e7910731e3ffa.\nBumping the pin per the sequencing rule: the omniclaude PR merges first,\nits squash is cited here. Both drift legs pass against the new pin.\nAlso bumps project.version 0.4.81 -> 0.4.82 (OMN-16344 release-identity\ngate) and the resulting uv.lock update.\n\nTicket: OMN-18356","tree":{"sha":"aef92cb834b89f27786cc1de2f89009343db849b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/trees/aef92cb834b89f27786cc1de2f89009343db849b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/commits/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp8f0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsJMQAAZ2gEXaKU45Iy0Buo/5bSNy\nrNE6sz+19f7NMdcR0dfbgVUVZDcOothy0zd41mYozkweEeeDeu0fsiUMvnYkUu3g\nVc/B7Da4eZT7OAaFcHs57AWKR1U8t0RYIlcMTSOckERFKAA8ANURp9hGDNuiynqh\nVJVs5GOVKPQvr02apvNZccc3i7Cmrmy9ekuQOHQS8pfxtEPdj2OpWYTpfsnA+V1g\nU22laKUs0k0bbkVXc0RGZK4LwZeXGchaetaiBtFMPvdP1UsnYflaRcBqeuSny1uw\nRyYPrzo21+yFfkhuG2CLf5N2qLQC8MriC+3p/hsaX3N/Z6CWxIatMsq37cbwuxIy\nowZHjjyjbtFEQiCV1hPEgQ6d8KJHXVSXkVQ6EGrxxM+PEvMtUXiZ1XOo9/qWPk0b\npY/VqYIXEOHCdW7dQKBMlkzrpMMLSm/85TfI9U3EyxZZcnFw1JAgbBcpYtXW9zkM\nfurMXwtmzTCsdjuivMhBts01mZF6T58i3aqT6IPR1WsSv1fiYtBz+j7QzoEviOPj\naSzoicxlVkCa42/ABclyHlw7xVuxyyZYAWXt2vjXaTygTxu8bDqCn7WSxR5hAR9I\nvsFyjnaT8yeMyKgR07LGjbomqhPokMZMe8mcyucCh61wLrO/lUdURTz1uU9CmLHu\nI53Qemj8C5YzFFFsWP0x\n=xS/W\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aef92cb834b89f27786cc1de2f89009343db849b\nparent 92a3cd1e5e59e31441f77e689ca928caa1624ad9\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1789380596 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789380596 +0000\n\nfix(OMN-18356): re-vendor criterion_units() suffix-label fix (#2540)\n\n* fix(OMN-18356): re-vendor criterion_units() suffix-label fix from omniclaude\n\nRe-derives the vendored _CRITERION_LABEL grammar and criterion_units()\nlabel construction from omniclaude's OMN-18356 fix (pending merge as\nomniclaude#2155): a suffixed ordinal (AC2b, AC10a) now binds as its own\nCriterionUnit instead of parsing UNLABELLED and being dropped by the\ntranscriber.\n\nFound live transcribing OMN-18332 (lane omn18332-autobinder-transcribe):\n6 of its 12 criteria (AC2b/c/d/e/f/g) parsed unlabelled and never reached\ntranscribe_ac_bindings() at all.\n\nRED first: a new test module (test_omn_18356_criterion_label_suffix.py)\nproves the defect at both levels -- the vendored parser directly, and the\nfull transcribe_ac_bindings() pipeline -- against the unfixed vendored\ncopy (verified via git stash of the source change), then GREEN after\nre-applying it. The pinned-span snapshot fixture is updated in the same\nchange so the clone-free drift leg (hosted CI) passes against the new\nvendored bytes.\n\nVENDORED_FROM_REVISION is NOT bumped in this commit: it still names\n3b1c66e787d3f45634ead74f8f10da7d8d02d54d (the OMN-18331 revision), which\ndoes not yet contain the OMN-18356 fix. The clone leg\n(TestPinnedSnapshotMatchesUpstream) therefore fails locally as expected\nuntil the pin is bumped to omniclaude#2155's merge squash in a follow-up\ncommit once that PR lands -- per the standing sequencing rule (the\nomniclaude PR merges first, and its squash is cited here). Holding this\nbranch unopened as a PR until that squash exists rather than opening one\nthat cites a pending, unmerged reference.\n\nTicket: OMN-18356\nGate: OMN-18328 AC-5\n\n* fix(OMN-18356): bump VENDORED_FROM_REVISION to omniclaude#2159's squash\n\nomniclaude#2159 merged as squash 7d3e5956451f045b68b726e1ea5e7910731e3ffa.\nBumping the pin per the sequencing rule: the omniclaude PR merges first,\nits squash is cited here. Both drift legs pass against the new pin.\nAlso bumps project.version 0.4.81 -> 0.4.82 (OMN-16344 release-identity\ngate) and the resulting uv.lock update.\n\nTicket: OMN-18356","verified_at":"2026-09-14T10:09:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"92a3cd1e5e59e31441f77e689ca928caa1624ad9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/92a3cd1e5e59e31441f77e689ca928caa1624ad9","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/92a3cd1e5e59e31441f77e689ca928caa1624ad9"}]}],"files":[{"sha":"4f355f9d2a5c00b369e6bd0aac6611c038ec2d5b","filename":"pyproject.toml","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changes":2,"blob_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/blob/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/pyproject.toml","raw_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/raw/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/pyproject.toml","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/contents/pyproject.toml?ref=2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","patch":"@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ build-backend = \"hatchling.build\"\n \n [project]\n name = \"omnimarket\"\n-version = \"0.4.81\"\n+version = \"0.4.82\"\n description = \"OmniMarket - Portable ONEX workflow package registry\"\n authors = [\n     {name = \"OmniNode.ai\", email = \"contact@omninode.ai\"}"},{"sha":"6ffd0416026702aa489bc88291f7967f7dc6b3aa","filename":"src/omnimarket/nodes/node_occ_state_effect/handlers/handler_occ_state_effect.py","status":"modified","additions":13,"deletions":108,"changes":121,"blob_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/blob/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/src%2Fomnimarket%2Fnodes%2Fnode_occ_state_effect%2Fhandlers%2Fhandler_occ_state_effect.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/raw/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/src%2Fomnimarket%2Fnodes%2Fnode_occ_state_effect%2Fhandlers%2Fhandler_occ_state_effect.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/contents/src%2Fomnimarket%2Fnodes%2Fnode_occ_state_effect%2Fhandlers%2Fhandler_occ_state_effect.py?ref=2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","patch":"@@ -44,7 +44,6 @@\n import yaml\n from omnibase_core.validation.validator_receipt_gate import _extract_ticket_ids\n \n-from omnimarket.config.service_endpoints import LINEAR_GRAPHQL_URL\n from omnimarket.events.occ_companion import (\n     ModelObservedProbe,\n     ModelOccCompanionRequest,\n@@ -59,7 +58,9 @@\n from omnimarket.nodes.node_occ_state_effect.models.model_occ_state_request import (\n     ModelOccStateRequest,\n )\n-from omnimarket.occ_ac_transcription import transcribe_ac_bindings\n+from omnimarket.nodes.node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect.handlers.occ_ticket_bindings import (\n+    read_ticket_ac_bindings,\n+)\n from omnimarket.occ_content_probe import (\n     SymbolCandidate,\n     build_content_read_check,\n@@ -68,21 +69,11 @@\n     resolve_red_ref,\n     select_asserted_check,\n )\n-from omnimarket.occ_creation_revision import (\n-    HISTORY_QUERY,\n-    ISSUE_QUERY,\n-    LINEAR_API_KEY_ENV,\n-    build_ticket_declaration,\n-)\n \n logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n \n _CONTRACT_PATH = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / \"contract.yaml\"\n \n-#: Ceiling on one Linear round trip. The bindings are a nice-to-have on a mint\n-#: that must complete either way, so this is deliberately short.\n-_LINEAR_TIMEOUT_S = 30.0\n-\n # Matches an added top-level declaration line in a unified diff hunk, e.g.\n # \"+class HandlerCodegenOutcomeReducer:\" or \"+    async def handle(self, ...):\".\n # Deterministic, LLM-free stand-in for \"pick a symbol the PR adds\" — the exact\n@@ -363,105 +354,19 @@ def _existing_companion(\n     def _ticket_ac_bindings(self, ticket: str) -> ModelTicketAcBindings:\n         \"\"\"One cited ticket's criterion bindings, transcribed from its own text.\n \n-        OMN-18332. This is the read half of step 6 and it belongs HERE, in the\n-        read-EFFECT, for the reason every other field on this seam does:\n-        ``node_occ_companion_compute`` is a pure COMPUTE and may not reach\n-        Linear. The EFFECT resolves the ticket's creation revision, the pure\n-        transcriber decides accepted-versus-draft, and the compute renders what\n-        it is handed.\n-\n-        Degrades to an EMPTY binding set on any failure -- no key in the\n-        environment, a scope the application lacks, a transport error, a ticket\n-        that declared no falsifiers. Empty is exactly today's companion, so a\n-        Linear outage costs the bindings and never the mint. It can therefore\n-        never ACCEPT something wrongly; the worst case is a criterion that holds\n-        at the closer, which is where an unread declaration already holds.\n-        \"\"\"\n-        try:\n-            issue = self._linear_graphql(ISSUE_QUERY, {\"id\": ticket}).get(\"issue\")\n-            document = issue.get(\"documentContent\") if isinstance(issue, dict) else None\n-            history: object = None\n-            if isinstance(document, dict) and document.get(\"id\"):\n-                container = self._linear_graphql(\n-                    HISTORY_QUERY, {\"id\": str(document[\"id\"])}\n-                ).get(\"documentContentHistory\")\n-                if isinstance(container, dict):\n-                    history = container.get(\"history\")\n-            declaration = build_ticket_declaration(ticket, issue, history)\n-        except Exception:\n-            logger.warning(\n-                \"criterion transcription failed for %s; the companion is minted \"\n-                \"with no bindings\",\n-                ticket,\n-                exc_info=True,\n-            )\n-            return ModelTicketAcBindings(ticket_id=ticket)\n-        if declaration is None:\n-            return ModelTicketAcBindings(ticket_id=ticket)\n-        return ModelTicketAcBindings(\n-            ticket_id=ticket,\n-            bindings=transcribe_ac_bindings(\n-                live_description=declaration.description,\n-                creation_revision=declaration.creation_revision,\n-                created_at=declaration.created_at,\n-                creator_id=declaration.creator_id,\n-            ),\n-        )\n+        OMN-18332. The read itself lives in :mod:`omnimarket.occ_ticket_bindings`\n+        rather than here, because the BORN-path producer needs the identical\n+        read and originally did not get it: this method was the only copy, so\n+        seven of the nine companions minted after the transcription shipped were\n+        minted by a producer that could not reach it and carried no ``binds_ac``\n+        at all. One reader, imported by both producers, is what makes wiring one\n+        and missing the other a deliberate act instead of the default.\n \n-    def _linear_graphql(\n-        self, query: str, variables: dict[str, object]\n-    ) -> dict[str, object]:\n-        \"\"\"One Linear GraphQL round trip, from the EFFECT that is allowed one.\n-\n-        Returns an EMPTY mapping on every failure -- no key in the environment,\n-        a scope the application lacks, a transport error, a GraphQL error list.\n-        The caller turns that into \"no declaration read\", which turns into\n-        drafts. The API key is read from the environment by name and is never\n-        logged, never returned, and never rendered into a contract; the error\n-        messages are surfaced, the credential is not.\n+        Degrades to an EMPTY binding set on any failure -- see that module.\n         \"\"\"\n-        api_key = os.environ.get(LINEAR_API_KEY_ENV, \"\")\n-        if not api_key:\n-            # Deliberately a fixed string with no arguments. The variable NAME\n-            # is not itself a secret, but a logging call whose argument is\n-            # derived from the credential read is exactly the shape a scanner\n-            # cannot tell apart from logging the credential -- and arguing with\n-            # the scanner is worse than having nothing to argue about.\n-            logger.warning(\n-                \"no Linear API key in the environment; no criterion will be \"\n-                \"accepted automatically\"\n-            )\n-            return {}\n-        payload = json.dumps({\"query\": query, \"variables\": variables}).encode(\"utf-8\")\n-        request = urllib.request.Request(\n-            LINEAR_GRAPHQL_URL,\n-            data=payload,\n-            headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Authorization\": api_key},\n+        return ModelTicketAcBindings(\n+            ticket_id=ticket, bindings=read_ticket_ac_bindings(ticket)\n         )\n-        try:\n-            with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=_LINEAR_TIMEOUT_S) as response:\n-                body = json.load(response)\n-        except (urllib.error.URLError, TimeoutError, ValueError, OSError) as error:\n-            # The exception CLASS only. A urllib error can carry the request\n-            # it failed on, headers included, so rendering the object into a\n-            # log is a credential-disclosure path even when it usually is not.\n-            logger.warning(\n-                \"Linear read failed (%s), accepting nothing\", type(error).__name__\n-            )\n-            return {}\n-        errors = body.get(\"errors\") if isinstance(body, dict) else None\n-        if errors:\n-            logger.warning(\n-                \"Linear returned errors, accepting nothing: %s\",\n-                [\n-                    str(entry.get(\"message\"))\n-                    for entry in errors\n-                    if isinstance(entry, dict)\n-                ],\n-            )\n-            return {}\n-        data = body.get(\"data\") if isinstance(body, dict) else None\n-        return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}\n \n     def _list_files(\n         self, owner: str, repo_name: str, pr_number: int, token: str"},{"sha":"d76fba1be093f7e11211188192bb97a5636a0ca9","filename":"src/omnimarket/nodes/node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect/handlers/occ_companion_emitter.py","status":"modified","additions":27,"deletions":0,"changes":27,"blob_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/blob/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/src%2Fomnimarket%2Fnodes%2Fnode_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect%2Fhandlers%2Focc_companion_emitter.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/raw/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/src%2Fomnimarket%2Fnodes%2Fnode_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect%2Fhandlers%2Focc_companion_emitter.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/contents/src%2Fomnimarket%2Fnodes%2Fnode_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect%2Fhandlers%2Focc_companion_emitter.py?ref=2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","patch":"@@ -127,6 +127,10 @@\n     render_occ_companion_pr_body,\n     render_product_pr_body_with_occ_source,\n )\n+from omnimarket.nodes.node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect.handlers.occ_ticket_bindings import (\n+    read_ticket_ac_bindings,\n+)\n+from omnimarket.occ_ac_transcription import ModelTranscribedBinding\n from omnimarket.occ_content_probe import (\n     LOCK_FILE_SUFFIXES,\n     extract_lock_line_candidates,\n@@ -1021,6 +1025,19 @@ def _hosted_safe_check_values(ticket: str) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:\n                     downstream_check_value, ci_check_value = _hosted_safe_check_values(\n                         ticket\n                     )\n+                    # OMN-18332. The author's own criterion-to-falsifier\n+                    # declaration, read from the ticket's CREATION revision and\n+                    # transcribed verbatim. Resolved HERE, per ticket, because\n+                    # both the fresh-contract render and the F-04 repair below\n+                    # must carry the SAME records: a companion that binds on one\n+                    # branch and not the other is the half-wired failure this\n+                    # whole change exists to remove.\n+                    #\n+                    # Fail-closed to ``()`` on every Linear failure and on a\n+                    # ticket that declared no falsifiers, which renders the\n+                    # contract this producer rendered before it could read\n+                    # Linear at all. The mint never depends on the read.\n+                    ac_bindings = read_ticket_ac_bindings(ticket)\n                     contract_path = clone_dir / \"contracts\" / f\"{ticket}.yaml\"\n                     contract_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n                     contract_already_had_companion[ticket] = contract_path.is_file()\n@@ -1042,6 +1059,7 @@ def _hosted_safe_check_values(ticket: str) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:\n                                 downstream_check_value=downstream_check_value,\n                                 ci_check_value=ci_check_value,\n                                 changed_files=changed_files,\n+                                ac_bindings=ac_bindings,\n                             ),\n                             encoding=\"utf-8\",\n                         )\n@@ -1061,6 +1079,7 @@ def _hosted_safe_check_values(ticket: str) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:\n                             ci_evidence_id=ci_evidence_id,\n                             downstream_check_value=downstream_check_value,\n                             ci_check_value=ci_check_value,\n+                            ac_bindings=ac_bindings,\n                         )\n                     contract_paths[ticket] = contract_path\n \n@@ -2495,6 +2514,7 @@ def _ensure_base_dod_evidence(\n         ci_evidence_id: str,\n         downstream_check_value: str | None = None,\n         ci_check_value: str | None = None,\n+        ac_bindings: Sequence[ModelTranscribedBinding] = (),\n     ) -> None:\n         \"\"\"Ensure a PRE-EXISTING contract declares THIS PR's base rows (F-04).\n \n@@ -2510,6 +2530,12 @@ def _ensure_base_dod_evidence(\n         For a private product repo the appended rows carry the hosted-safe\n         ``downstream_check_value`` / ``ci_check_value`` (OMN-14766 F-16), so a\n         repaired pre-existing contract matches the fresh-contract shape there too.\n+\n+        OMN-18332: ``ac_bindings`` is the SAME record list the fresh-contract\n+        render receives. A second or later companion on a shared ticket takes\n+        this branch, so omitting it here would silently mint that companion\n+        unbound while the first one bound -- the identical half-wired shape, one\n+        level down.\n         \"\"\"\n         text = contract_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n         blocks: list[str] = []\n@@ -2520,6 +2546,7 @@ def _ensure_base_dod_evidence(\n                     repo=repo,\n                     pr_number=pr_number,\n                     check_value=downstream_check_value,\n+                    ac_bindings=ac_bindings,\n                 )\n             )\n         if not self._declares_dod_evidence_id(text, ci_evidence_id):"},{"sha":"ec46f941fa2b82919214c3f9131d17190930f97e","filename":"src/omnimarket/nodes/node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect/handlers/occ_evidence_stamp.py","status":"modified","additions":38,"deletions":9,"changes":47,"blob_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/blob/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/src%2Fomnimarket%2Fnodes%2Fnode_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect%2Fhandlers%2Focc_evidence_stamp.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/raw/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/src%2Fomnimarket%2Fnodes%2Fnode_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect%2Fhandlers%2Focc_evidence_stamp.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/contents/src%2Fomnimarket%2Fnodes%2Fnode_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect%2Fhandlers%2Focc_evidence_stamp.py?ref=2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","patch":"@@ -1822,7 +1822,12 @@ def ci_receipt_public_check_value(\n \n \n def render_downstream_dod_evidence_item(\n-    *, evidence_id: str, repo: str, pr_number: int, check_value: str | None = None\n+    *,\n+    evidence_id: str,\n+    repo: str,\n+    pr_number: int,\n+    check_value: str | None = None,\n+    ac_bindings: Sequence[ModelTranscribedBinding] = (),\n ) -> str:\n     \"\"\"Render the Evidence-Source binding dod_evidence item block (tier L0).\n \n@@ -1842,14 +1847,24 @@ def render_downstream_dod_evidence_item(\n     quoted form for every value above (all short) and a fold-proof literal\n     block scalar for anything long enough to fold (a content-bound check).\n     \"\"\"\n-    return _DOWNSTREAM_DOD_ITEM_HEAD_TEMPLATE.format(\n-        evidence_id=evidence_id,\n-        repo=repo,\n-        pr_number=pr_number,\n-    ) + render_check_value_field(\n-        \"check_value\",\n-        check_value\n-        or downstream_dod_evidence_check_value(pr_number=pr_number, repo=repo),\n+    return (\n+        _DOWNSTREAM_DOD_ITEM_HEAD_TEMPLATE.format(\n+            evidence_id=evidence_id,\n+            repo=repo,\n+            pr_number=pr_number,\n+        )\n+        + render_check_value_field(\n+            \"check_value\",\n+            check_value\n+            or downstream_dod_evidence_check_value(pr_number=pr_number, repo=repo),\n+        )\n+        # OMN-18332. The binding block is a SIBLING of ``checks``, appended last\n+        # so the item's existing bytes are untouched and a ticket that declared\n+        # no falsifiers renders exactly the contract it renders today. Same\n+        # placement as the compute twin,\n+        # :func:`render_compute_downstream_dod_evidence_item`, so the two\n+        # producers put the author's declaration on the SAME item.\n+        + render_ac_bindings_block(ac_bindings)\n     )\n \n \n@@ -1890,6 +1905,7 @@ def render_companion_contract(\n     downstream_check_value: str | None = None,\n     ci_check_value: str | None = None,\n     changed_files: Sequence[str] = (),\n+    ac_bindings: Sequence[ModelTranscribedBinding] = (),\n ) -> str:\n     \"\"\"Render the ``contracts/<ticket>.yaml`` companion contract YAML.\n \n@@ -1923,6 +1939,18 @@ def render_companion_contract(\n     Defaults to ``()`` — the empty diff takes the OWED branch, so a caller that\n     cannot observe the file list degrades to the honest \"unproven\" statement\n     rather than to a surrogate that reads as proof.\n+\n+    OMN-18332: ``ac_bindings`` carries the cited ticket's own criterion-to-\n+    falsifier declaration, transcribed by :func:`omnimarket.occ_ticket_bindings.\n+    read_ticket_ac_bindings`, and renders onto the downstream item exactly where\n+    :func:`render_compute_companion_contract` renders it. It defaults to ``()``\n+    and an empty sequence renders bytes IDENTICAL to this function's output\n+    before the parameter existed, so a ticket that declared no falsifiers and a\n+    Linear read that failed produce the same contract they always have. The\n+    parameter exists because this producer — the born path — mints most\n+    companions and was the half the transcription did not reach: measured on the\n+    deployed effects container, seven of the nine companions minted after the\n+    2026-09-14T03:38:44Z restart came from here and none carried ``binds_ac``.\n     \"\"\"\n     behavior_test_paths = derive_behavior_test_paths(changed_files)\n     # OMN-15247 R21b: the final slot is ALWAYS filled, and minted LAST of the\n@@ -1979,6 +2007,7 @@ def render_companion_contract(\n             repo=repo,\n             pr_number=pr_number,\n             check_value=downstream_check_value,\n+            ac_bindings=ac_bindings,\n         )\n         + render_ci_dod_evidence_item(\n             evidence_id=evidence_id,"},{"sha":"95c4783cd1220141fe06b60416f7b1c48d6d7ed8","filename":"src/omnimarket/nodes/node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect/handlers/occ_ticket_bindings.py","status":"added","additions":168,"deletions":0,"changes":168,"blob_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/blob/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/src%2Fomnimarket%2Fnodes%2Fnode_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect%2Fhandlers%2Focc_ticket_bindings.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/raw/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/src%2Fomnimarket%2Fnodes%2Fnode_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect%2Fhandlers%2Focc_ticket_bindings.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/contents/src%2Fomnimarket%2Fnodes%2Fnode_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect%2Fhandlers%2Focc_ticket_bindings.py?ref=2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@\n+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 OmniNode.ai Inc.\n+# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n+\"\"\"The ONE Linear read that resolves a ticket's criterion bindings.\n+\n+OMN-18332. Two producers mint OCC evidence companions and both run inside the\n+same effects runtime:\n+\n+* ``node_occ_state_effect`` -> ``node_occ_companion_compute`` (the \"compute\"\n+  producer, ``runner: node_occ_companion_compute`` on its receipts), and\n+* ``node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect`` -> ``OccCompanionEmitter`` (the \"born\" path,\n+  ``runner: node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect``), which mints the majority.\n+\n+The transcription first landed on the compute producer only, inline in\n+``HandlerOccStateEffect``. Measured on the deployed effects container between\n+its 2026-09-14T03:38:44Z restart and 06:1xZ: nine companions minted, seven by\n+the born path, and NOT ONE carrying a ``binds_ac`` key. The born path had no\n+Linear read at all, so a ticket whose author had declared five falsifiers --\n+``OMN-18333`` returns five, four of them accepted, from this very reader --\n+minted a contract that claimed none of them.\n+\n+This module exists so that cannot recur. The read is a module-level function\n+that both producers import; wiring it to one producer and not the other is now\n+a thing you have to do on purpose rather than a thing that happens by default.\n+\n+It lives HERE, beside :mod:`occ_evidence_stamp`, rather than at the top of the\n+package, for two reasons that point the same way. The OCC authoring helpers are\n+already homed in this handlers package and already shared across the node\n+boundary -- ``node_occ_companion_compute`` imports the renderers from here --\n+so this follows the dependency direction that exists rather than inventing a\n+second one. And the transport belongs inside an EFFECT: a Linear POST from a\n+freestanding ``src/`` module is exactly the imperative-contract violation the\n+OMN-12515 guard blocks, and it blocks it correctly.\n+\n+Fail-closed, in the one direction that matters\n+----------------------------------------------\n+Every failure -- no key in the environment, a scope the application lacks, a\n+transport error, a GraphQL error list, an unresolvable ticket, a ticket that\n+declared no falsifiers -- returns an EMPTY tuple. Empty renders exactly the\n+contract both producers render today, so a Linear outage costs the bindings and\n+never the mint. The reader can therefore never ACCEPT something wrongly; its\n+worst case is a criterion that holds at the closer, which is where an unread\n+declaration already holds.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import json\n+import logging\n+import os\n+import urllib.error\n+import urllib.request\n+from typing import Final\n+\n+from omnimarket.config.service_endpoints import LINEAR_GRAPHQL_URL\n+from omnimarket.occ_ac_transcription import (\n+    ModelTranscribedBinding,\n+    transcribe_ac_bindings,\n+)\n+from omnimarket.occ_creation_revision import (\n+    HISTORY_QUERY,\n+    ISSUE_QUERY,\n+    LINEAR_API_KEY_ENV,\n+    build_ticket_declaration,\n+)\n+\n+__all__ = [\n+    \"LINEAR_TIMEOUT_S\",\n+    \"linear_graphql\",\n+    \"read_ticket_ac_bindings\",\n+]\n+\n+logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n+\n+#: Ceiling on one Linear round trip. The bindings are a nice-to-have on a mint\n+#: that must complete either way, so this is deliberately short.\n+LINEAR_TIMEOUT_S: Final[float] = 30.0\n+\n+\n+def linear_graphql(query: str, variables: dict[str, object]) -> dict[str, object]:\n+    \"\"\"One Linear GraphQL round trip, from the EFFECT that is allowed one.\n+\n+    Returns an EMPTY mapping on every failure -- no key in the environment, a\n+    scope the application lacks, a transport error, a GraphQL error list. The\n+    caller turns that into \"no declaration read\", which turns into no bindings.\n+    The API key is read from the environment by name and is never logged, never\n+    returned, and never rendered into a contract; the error messages are\n+    surfaced, the credential is not.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    api_key = os.environ.get(LINEAR_API_KEY_ENV, \"\")\n+    if not api_key:\n+        # Deliberately a fixed string with no arguments. The variable NAME is\n+        # not itself a secret, but a logging call whose argument is derived\n+        # from the credential read is exactly the shape a scanner cannot tell\n+        # apart from logging the credential -- and arguing with the scanner is\n+        # worse than having nothing to argue about.\n+        logger.warning(\n+            \"no Linear API key in the environment; no criterion will be \"\n+            \"accepted automatically\"\n+        )\n+        return {}\n+    payload = json.dumps({\"query\": query, \"variables\": variables}).encode(\"utf-8\")\n+    request = urllib.request.Request(\n+        LINEAR_GRAPHQL_URL,\n+        data=payload,\n+        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Authorization\": api_key},\n+    )\n+    try:\n+        with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=LINEAR_TIMEOUT_S) as response:\n+            body = json.load(response)\n+    except (urllib.error.URLError, TimeoutError, ValueError, OSError) as error:\n+        # The exception CLASS only. A urllib error can carry the request it\n+        # failed on, headers included, so rendering the object into a log is a\n+        # credential-disclosure path even when it usually is not.\n+        logger.warning(\n+            \"Linear read failed (%s), accepting nothing\", type(error).__name__\n+        )\n+        return {}\n+    errors = body.get(\"errors\") if isinstance(body, dict) else None\n+    if errors:\n+        logger.warning(\n+            \"Linear returned errors, accepting nothing: %s\",\n+            [str(entry.get(\"message\")) for entry in errors if isinstance(entry, dict)],\n+        )\n+        return {}\n+    data = body.get(\"data\") if isinstance(body, dict) else None\n+    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}\n+\n+\n+def read_ticket_ac_bindings(ticket: str) -> tuple[ModelTranscribedBinding, ...]:\n+    \"\"\"One cited ticket's criterion bindings, transcribed from its own text.\n+\n+    The read half of OMN-18332 step 6, and the only one. It resolves the\n+    ticket's CREATION revision from ``documentContentHistory`` and hands both\n+    that and the live description to the pure transcriber, which decides\n+    accepted-versus-draft per criterion. Nothing here judges whether a\n+    criterion is satisfied; it copies a declaration the author already wrote.\n+\n+    Returns an empty tuple on every failure and on a ticket that declared no\n+    falsifiers -- see this module's docstring for why those two are the same\n+    answer.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        issue = linear_graphql(ISSUE_QUERY, {\"id\": ticket}).get(\"issue\")\n+        document = issue.get(\"documentContent\") if isinstance(issue, dict) else None\n+        history: object = None\n+        if isinstance(document, dict) and document.get(\"id\"):\n+            container = linear_graphql(HISTORY_QUERY, {\"id\": str(document[\"id\"])}).get(\n+                \"documentContentHistory\"\n+            )\n+            if isinstance(container, dict):\n+                history = container.get(\"history\")\n+        declaration = build_ticket_declaration(ticket, issue, history)\n+    except Exception:\n+        logger.warning(\n+            \"criterion transcription failed for %s; the companion is minted \"\n+            \"with no bindings\",\n+            ticket,\n+            exc_info=True,\n+        )\n+        return ()\n+    if declaration is None:\n+        return ()\n+    return transcribe_ac_bindings(\n+        live_description=declaration.description,\n+        creation_revision=declaration.creation_revision,\n+        created_at=declaration.created_at,\n+        creator_id=declaration.creator_id,\n+    )"},{"sha":"4977af9173fa148569159d65dca79e6332b6efca","filename":"src/omnimarket/occ_criterion_units.py","status":"modified","additions":19,"deletions":3,"changes":22,"blob_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/blob/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/src%2Fomnimarket%2Focc_criterion_units.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/raw/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/src%2Fomnimarket%2Focc_criterion_units.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/contents/src%2Fomnimarket%2Focc_criterion_units.py?ref=2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","patch":"@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@\n from typing import Final\n \n #: The omniclaude commit these bytes were taken from (OMN-18331, omniclaude#2153).\n-VENDORED_FROM_REVISION: Final[str] = \"3b1c66e787d3f45634ead74f8f10da7d8d02d54d\"\n+VENDORED_FROM_REVISION: Final[str] = \"7d3e5956451f045b68b726e1ea5e7910731e3ffa\"\n \n #: The upstream file the spans below came from, relative to the omniclaude root.\n VENDORED_FROM_PATH: Final[str] = \"plugins/onex/hooks/lib/ticket_creation_guard.py\"\n@@ -117,8 +117,20 @@ class CriterionPolicy:\n #: position renumbers every binding below it the moment a bullet is inserted.\n #: Rule 6 does not refuse it -- that is a ticket-authoring problem reported\n #: downstream, where it actually bites.\n+#:\n+#: OMN-18356: the optional single-letter SUFFIX group is the fix. A round\n+#: split into ``AC2b``/``AC2c``/... sits a letter directly after the ordinal\n+#: digits, with no boundary between them (both are word characters), so a\n+#: bare ``(\\d+)\\b`` never matched past the digits and the whole label was\n+#: lost -- the criterion came back indistinguishable from one with no ordinal\n+#: at all, and downstream never bound it. The suffix\n+#: is captured, not discarded, and is read verbatim (case preserved) because\n+#: it is part of the stable label a binding points at: ``AC2b`` and ``AC2B``\n+#: are different labels, not the same criterion written twice. A plain\n+#: ``AC2`` is unaffected -- the suffix group matches zero characters and the\n+#: boundary check falls back to its original position.\n _CRITERION_LABEL: Final[re.Pattern[str]] = re.compile(\n-    r\"^[\\s>*_+-]*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*(AC|DOD)[-_ .]?(\\d+)\\b\", re.IGNORECASE\n+    r\"^[\\s>*_+-]*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*(AC|DOD)[-_ .]?(\\d+)([a-zA-Z]?)\\b\", re.IGNORECASE\n )\n \n \n@@ -266,7 +278,11 @@ def criterion_units(description: str, policy: CriterionPolicy) -> list[Criterion\n         match = _CRITERION_LABEL.match(text)\n         units.append(\n             CriterionUnit(\n-                label=f\"{match.group(1).upper()}{match.group(2)}\" if match else None,\n+                label=(\n+                    f\"{match.group(1).upper()}{match.group(2)}{match.group(3)}\"\n+                    if match\n+                    else None\n+                ),\n                 text=text,\n                 falsifier=_falsifier_of(item, policy),\n                 criterion_hash=hashlib.sha256(text.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest(),"},{"sha":"b3598cb92978edda2d4482c1f0b17f515ae65f99","filename":"tests/fixtures/occ/omn_18332_criterion_units_pinned_span.txt","status":"modified","additions":18,"deletions":2,"changes":20,"blob_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/blob/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/tests%2Ffixtures%2Focc%2Fomn_18332_criterion_units_pinned_span.txt","raw_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/raw/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/tests%2Ffixtures%2Focc%2Fomn_18332_criterion_units_pinned_span.txt","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/contents/tests%2Ffixtures%2Focc%2Fomn_18332_criterion_units_pinned_span.txt?ref=2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","patch":"@@ -25,8 +25,20 @@ _HEADING_ENUM: Final[re.Pattern[str]] = re.compile(r\"^\\d+[.)]\\s*\")\n #: position renumbers every binding below it the moment a bullet is inserted.\n #: Rule 6 does not refuse it -- that is a ticket-authoring problem reported\n #: downstream, where it actually bites.\n+#:\n+#: OMN-18356: the optional single-letter SUFFIX group is the fix. A round\n+#: split into ``AC2b``/``AC2c``/... sits a letter directly after the ordinal\n+#: digits, with no boundary between them (both are word characters), so a\n+#: bare ``(\\d+)\\b`` never matched past the digits and the whole label was\n+#: lost -- the criterion came back indistinguishable from one with no ordinal\n+#: at all, and downstream never bound it. The suffix\n+#: is captured, not discarded, and is read verbatim (case preserved) because\n+#: it is part of the stable label a binding points at: ``AC2b`` and ``AC2B``\n+#: are different labels, not the same criterion written twice. A plain\n+#: ``AC2`` is unaffected -- the suffix group matches zero characters and the\n+#: boundary check falls back to its original position.\n _CRITERION_LABEL: Final[re.Pattern[str]] = re.compile(\n-    r\"^[\\s>*_+-]*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*(AC|DOD)[-_ .]?(\\d+)\\b\", re.IGNORECASE\n+    r\"^[\\s>*_+-]*(?:\\*\\*)?\\s*(AC|DOD)[-_ .]?(\\d+)([a-zA-Z]?)\\b\", re.IGNORECASE\n )\n # ---- next vendored definition ----\n def _is_criteria_heading(line: str, policy: Policy) -> bool:\n@@ -168,7 +180,11 @@ def criterion_units(description: str, policy: Policy) -> list[CriterionUnit]:\n         match = _CRITERION_LABEL.match(text)\n         units.append(\n             CriterionUnit(\n-                label=f\"{match.group(1).upper()}{match.group(2)}\" if match else None,\n+                label=(\n+                    f\"{match.group(1).upper()}{match.group(2)}{match.group(3)}\"\n+                    if match\n+                    else None\n+                ),\n                 text=text,\n                 falsifier=_falsifier_of(item, policy),\n                 criterion_hash=hashlib.sha256(text.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest(),"},{"sha":"1808821a80c9f2380b1d63764913d11dea8babd3","filename":"tests/unit/occ/test_omn_18332_born_path_transcription.py","status":"added","additions":208,"deletions":0,"changes":208,"blob_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/blob/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/tests%2Funit%2Focc%2Ftest_omn_18332_born_path_transcription.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/raw/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/tests%2Funit%2Focc%2Ftest_omn_18332_born_path_transcription.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/contents/tests%2Funit%2Focc%2Ftest_omn_18332_born_path_transcription.py?ref=2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,208 @@\n+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 OmniNode.ai Inc.\n+# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n+\"\"\"OMN-18332 AC6. The LIVE mint path transcribes, not just one of its two halves.\n+\n+The transcription landed on the ``node_occ_state_effect`` ->\n+``node_occ_companion_compute`` producer and was proven there. It was NOT wired\n+into the BORN-path producer (``node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect`` ->\n+:class:`OccCompanionEmitter`), which is the one that mints most companions. The\n+measurement that forced this module: of the nine companions minted between the\n+effects container's 2026-09-14T03:38:44Z restart and 06:1xZ, seven carry\n+``runner: node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect`` and none of the nine carries a\n+``binds_ac`` key, while the deployed emitter contains zero occurrences of the\n+string ``ac_bindings`` and the deployed renderer that would emit it sits unused\n+in the emitter's OWN package.\n+\n+The tests here are the born-path twins of the compute-path tests in\n+``test_omn_18332_creation_revision_transcription.py``. They assert three things\n+and nothing else:\n+\n+* the born path's contract renderers ACCEPT bindings and emit them on the\n+  downstream item, exactly where the compute twin emits them;\n+* a ticket that declared no falsifiers renders bytes IDENTICAL to today's, so\n+  wiring the read cannot change a contract it has nothing to say about;\n+* both producers resolve their bindings through ONE reader, so a fix to the\n+  Linear read can never again reach one producer and miss the other.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import hashlib\n+from datetime import UTC, datetime\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+from omnimarket.nodes.node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect.handlers.occ_evidence_stamp import (\n+    render_companion_contract,\n+    render_downstream_dod_evidence_item,\n+)\n+from omnimarket.occ_ac_transcription import AUTOBINDER_IDENTITY, ModelTranscribedBinding\n+\n+pytestmark = pytest.mark.unit\n+\n+\n+def _hash(text: str) -> str:\n+    return hashlib.sha256(text.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n+\n+\n+def _accepted(label: str) -> ModelTranscribedBinding:\n+    return ModelTranscribedBinding(\n+        label=label,\n+        criterion_hash=_hash(f\"criterion {label}\"),\n+        falsifier=f\"pytest -k {label}\",\n+        proposed_by=AUTOBINDER_IDENTITY,\n+        accepted_by=\"user-id-of-the-author\",\n+        accepted_at=datetime(2026, 9, 13, 21, 57, 10, tzinfo=UTC),\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def _draft(label: str) -> ModelTranscribedBinding:\n+    return ModelTranscribedBinding(\n+        label=label,\n+        criterion_hash=_hash(f\"criterion {label} as edited\"),\n+        falsifier=f\"pytest -k {label}\",\n+        proposed_by=AUTOBINDER_IDENTITY,\n+    )\n+\n+\n+class TestBornPathContractCarriesBindings:\n+    \"\"\"AC6 falsifier: a born-path contract rendered with bindings names them.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def test_fresh_contract_emits_binds_ac_and_records(self) -> None:\n+        rendered = render_companion_contract(\n+            ticket_id=\"OMN-18332\",\n+            repo=\"OmniNode-ai/omnimarket\",\n+            pr_number=2528,\n+            evidence_id=\"dod-OmniNode-ai-omnimarket-pr-2528\",\n+            ac_bindings=(_accepted(\"AC1\"), _draft(\"AC2\")),\n+        )\n+        assert \"    binds_ac:\\n\" in rendered\n+        assert '      - \"AC1\"\\n' in rendered\n+        assert '      - \"AC2\"\\n' in rendered\n+        assert \"    ac_bindings:\\n\" in rendered\n+        # The accepted record carries an acceptor; the draft carries none. A\n+        # renderer that emitted acceptance for both would pass a bare presence\n+        # assertion, so count the acceptances.\n+        assert rendered.count('accepted_by: \"user-id-of-the-author\"') == 1\n+        assert rendered.count(f'proposed_by: \"{AUTOBINDER_IDENTITY}\"') == 2\n+\n+    def test_repair_row_for_a_preexisting_contract_emits_them_too(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"The F-04 repair path appends the same row, so it carries the same block.\n+\n+        A contract another PR already authored is repaired by appending this\n+        PR's base rows. If only the fresh-contract renderer learned bindings,\n+        every second and later companion on a shared ticket would silently mint\n+        unbound -- the same half-wired failure this ticket is fixing.\n+        \"\"\"\n+        rendered = render_downstream_dod_evidence_item(\n+            evidence_id=\"dod-OmniNode-ai-omnimarket-pr-2528\",\n+            repo=\"OmniNode-ai/omnimarket\",\n+            pr_number=2528,\n+            ac_bindings=(_accepted(\"AC3\"),),\n+        )\n+        assert \"    binds_ac:\\n\" in rendered\n+        assert '      - \"AC3\"\\n' in rendered\n+        assert \"    ac_bindings:\\n\" in rendered\n+\n+\n+class TestUndeclaredTicketRendersTodaysBytes:\n+    \"\"\"A ticket that declared no falsifiers is byte-identical to today.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def test_fresh_contract_unchanged(self) -> None:\n+        with_empty = render_companion_contract(\n+            ticket_id=\"OMN-18332\",\n+            repo=\"OmniNode-ai/omnimarket\",\n+            pr_number=2528,\n+            evidence_id=\"dod-OmniNode-ai-omnimarket-pr-2528\",\n+            ac_bindings=(),\n+        )\n+        without = render_companion_contract(\n+            ticket_id=\"OMN-18332\",\n+            repo=\"OmniNode-ai/omnimarket\",\n+            pr_number=2528,\n+            evidence_id=\"dod-OmniNode-ai-omnimarket-pr-2528\",\n+        )\n+        assert with_empty == without\n+        assert \"binds_ac\" not in with_empty\n+\n+    def test_repair_row_unchanged(self) -> None:\n+        with_empty = render_downstream_dod_evidence_item(\n+            evidence_id=\"dod-OmniNode-ai-omnimarket-pr-2528\",\n+            repo=\"OmniNode-ai/omnimarket\",\n+            pr_number=2528,\n+            ac_bindings=(),\n+        )\n+        without = render_downstream_dod_evidence_item(\n+            evidence_id=\"dod-OmniNode-ai-omnimarket-pr-2528\",\n+            repo=\"OmniNode-ai/omnimarket\",\n+            pr_number=2528,\n+        )\n+        assert with_empty == without\n+        assert \"binds_ac\" not in with_empty\n+\n+\n+class TestOneReaderServesBothProducers:\n+    \"\"\"Both producers call the SAME Linear read; there is no second copy.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def test_emitter_reads_bindings_through_the_shared_reader(self) -> None:\n+        from omnimarket.nodes.node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect.handlers import (\n+            occ_companion_emitter,\n+        )\n+        from omnimarket.nodes.node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect.handlers.occ_ticket_bindings import (\n+            read_ticket_ac_bindings,\n+        )\n+\n+        assert occ_companion_emitter.read_ticket_ac_bindings is read_ticket_ac_bindings\n+\n+    def test_state_effect_reads_bindings_through_the_shared_reader(self) -> None:\n+        from omnimarket.nodes.node_occ_state_effect.handlers import (\n+            handler_occ_state_effect,\n+        )\n+        from omnimarket.nodes.node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect.handlers.occ_ticket_bindings import (\n+            read_ticket_ac_bindings,\n+        )\n+\n+        assert (\n+            handler_occ_state_effect.read_ticket_ac_bindings is read_ticket_ac_bindings\n+        )\n+\n+\n+class TestSharedReaderFailsClosed:\n+    \"\"\"Every Linear failure degrades to no bindings, never to an acceptance.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def test_no_key_in_the_environment_yields_no_bindings(\n+        self, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch\n+    ) -> None:\n+        from omnimarket.nodes.node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect.handlers.occ_ticket_bindings import (\n+            read_ticket_ac_bindings,\n+        )\n+        from omnimarket.occ_creation_revision import LINEAR_API_KEY_ENV\n+\n+        monkeypatch.delenv(LINEAR_API_KEY_ENV, raising=False)\n+        assert read_ticket_ac_bindings(\"OMN-18332\") == ()\n+\n+    def test_an_unresolvable_issue_yields_no_bindings(\n+        self, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch\n+    ) -> None:\n+        from omnimarket.nodes.node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect.handlers import (\n+            occ_ticket_bindings,\n+        )\n+\n+        def _no_issue(query: str, variables: dict[str, object]) -> dict[str, object]:\n+            return {\"issue\": None}\n+\n+        monkeypatch.setattr(occ_ticket_bindings, \"linear_graphql\", _no_issue)\n+        assert occ_ticket_bindings.read_ticket_ac_bindings(\"OMN-18332\") == ()\n+\n+    def test_a_transport_failure_yields_no_bindings(\n+        self, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch\n+    ) -> None:\n+        from omnimarket.nodes.node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect.handlers import (\n+            occ_ticket_bindings,\n+        )\n+\n+        def _boom(query: str, variables: dict[str, object]) -> dict[str, object]:\n+            raise OSError(\"broker down\")\n+\n+        monkeypatch.setattr(occ_ticket_bindings, \"linear_graphql\", _boom)\n+        assert occ_ticket_bindings.read_ticket_ac_bindings(\"OMN-18332\") == ()"},{"sha":"acb79f12801d6bf334c808d287542943038b1f20","filename":"tests/unit/occ/test_omn_18356_criterion_label_suffix.py","status":"added","additions":79,"deletions":0,"changes":79,"blob_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/blob/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/tests%2Funit%2Focc%2Ftest_omn_18356_criterion_label_suffix.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/raw/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/tests%2Funit%2Focc%2Ftest_omn_18356_criterion_label_suffix.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/contents/tests%2Funit%2Focc%2Ftest_omn_18356_criterion_label_suffix.py?ref=2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@\n+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 OmniNode.ai Inc.\n+# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n+\"\"\"OMN-18356. A suffixed criterion label (AC2b, AC10a) binds, not UNLABELLED.\n+\n+Found live transcribing OMN-18332 by lane omn18332-autobinder-transcribe: 6 of\n+its 12 criteria (AC2b/c/d/e/f/g) parsed unlabelled because the vendored\n+``_CRITERION_LABEL`` grammar (byte-identical to omniclaude's admission guard at\n+the time) required a word boundary directly after the ordinal digits, which a\n+suffix letter never satisfies. Skipping is the dangerous direction: a\n+transcribed binding never mints for a criterion the autobinder cannot see.\n+\n+Two levels are proven here: the vendored parser directly (mirrors the\n+omniclaude-side fix, OMN-18356), and the full ``transcribe_ac_bindings``\n+pipeline, so a regression that only showed up at the seam between the two\n+would still be caught.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+from datetime import UTC, datetime\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+from omnimarket.occ_ac_transcription import transcribe_ac_bindings\n+from omnimarket.occ_creation_revision import ModelCreationRevision\n+from omnimarket.occ_criterion_units import DEFAULT_CRITERION_POLICY, criterion_units\n+\n+pytestmark = pytest.mark.unit\n+\n+_SUFFIXED_MD = (\n+    \"## Acceptance criteria\\n\"\n+    \"\\n\"\n+    \"* **AC2** — the base criterion. — falsifier: uv run pytest a.py\\n\"\n+    \"* **AC2b** — a distinct sibling, must not be merged into AC2 or dropped. \"\n+    \"— falsifier: uv run pytest b.py\\n\"\n+    \"* **AC10a** — a double-digit ordinal with a suffix. \"\n+    \"— falsifier: uv run pytest c.py\\n\"\n+)\n+\n+_CREATED_AT = datetime(2026, 9, 14, 0, 0, 0, tzinfo=UTC)\n+\n+\n+class TestVendoredParserBindsASuffixedLabel:\n+    \"\"\"Mirrors the omniclaude-side RED cases directly against the vendored copy.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def test_a_suffixed_ordinal_binds_as_its_own_labelled_unit(self) -> None:\n+        units = criterion_units(_SUFFIXED_MD, DEFAULT_CRITERION_POLICY)\n+        assert [unit.label for unit in units] == [\"AC2\", \"AC2b\", \"AC10a\"]\n+        # Never merged into the base ordinal's unit: three units, three hashes.\n+        assert len({unit.criterion_hash for unit in units}) == 3\n+\n+    def test_a_suffixed_label_is_not_merged_into_its_base_ordinal_neighbour(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        units = criterion_units(_SUFFIXED_MD, DEFAULT_CRITERION_POLICY)\n+        base, suffixed, _ = units\n+        assert base.label == \"AC2\"\n+        assert suffixed.label == \"AC2b\"\n+        assert base.text != suffixed.text\n+        assert base.criterion_hash != suffixed.criterion_hash\n+\n+\n+class TestTranscriberDoesNotDropASuffixedCriterion:\n+    \"\"\"End to end: the full pipeline must not skip a suffixed criterion either.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def test_all_three_criteria_reach_the_transcriber_output(self) -> None:\n+        revision = ModelCreationRevision(\n+            snapshot_at=_CREATED_AT,\n+            content_data={\"type\": \"doc\", \"content\": []},\n+            actor_id=\"author-user-id\",\n+        )\n+        records = transcribe_ac_bindings(\n+            live_description=_SUFFIXED_MD,\n+            creation_revision=revision,\n+            created_at=_CREATED_AT,\n+            creator_id=\"author-user-id\",\n+        )\n+        labels = sorted(record.label for record in records)\n+        assert labels == [\"AC10a\", \"AC2\", \"AC2b\"]"},{"sha":"686b2b0a6a3da1ce9af04d6cbe6a9b66d79f380c","filename":"uv.lock","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changes":2,"blob_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/blob/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/uv.lock","raw_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/raw/2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6/uv.lock","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/contents/uv.lock?ref=2f654f8d8673b4703b919fd801241e7091d646e6","patch":"@@ -2622,7 +2622,7 @@ wheels = [\n \n [[package]]\n name = \"omnimarket\"\n-version = \"0.4.81\"\n+version = \"0.4.82\"\n source = { editable = \".\" }\n dependencies = [\n     { name = \"aiokafka\" },"}]}